  "scope": "Isolated fresh A296 per-worker/per-hour fixed64KiB owned record blocks replace geometrically growing mapped row vectors, retaining every full32-bit packed row/19-bit latency escape/ID/error and all original parsing/grouping/quantile/output/PGO. No indexed input reparse, per-endpoint node pool, 3-byte truncation or seed recognition. Explicit placement-new default initialization starts trivial Block/array lifetime; only appended initialized prefix is read. Each append publishes count after value write; iterator handles empty/final/full/partial block without end dereference. Owned blocks free via same original MappedAllocator at completed-hour swap; no global/host/harness/counter changes. Source growth and block syscall/iterator cost may outweigh lower capacity/copy/RSS; native full screen first, then strict independent prefix/guard/empty/allocation-failure/move/swap/lifetime/release/cross-thread models and main/GCC/image/default/Make/source/actual proof before promotion. Original selected295 remains unchanged.",
